    "result_text": "The change is complete and the build is green (`Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, `BUILD SUCCESS`).\n\n## What I did\n\nUnified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`, and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**Identifier assignment** \u2014 Replaced `AssignCustomerCode` with `AssignMemberId` (`src/main/.../function/owner/AssignMemberId.java`, wired into `owners.POST.yml` as step `assignMemberId`). It builds `region + fy + hash8`, appends a Luhn `CHK` over that core, and applies **collision handling to the memberId** (`-<n>` suffix on conflict) \u2014 reusing the existing `Locality`, `FiscalYear.yearSegment`, `OwnerIdentity.customerHash` (SHA-256 over normalized telephone + last name, first 8 upper-hex) and `CheckDigit`.\n\n**Model & persistence** \u2014 `Owner.customerCode` \u2192 `memberId` (`member_id` column, widened to `VARCHAR(32)` across the hsqldb/h2/mysql/postgres schemas).\n\n**API** \u2014 `openapi.yml` now exposes a single `memberId` field; `customerCode`, `membershipNumber` and `checkDigit` are gone (the generated `OwnerDto` regenerates accordingly; the acceptance test's `!has(\"customerCode\") && !has(\"membershipNumber\")` passes).\n\n**Consumers now reference the memberId:**\n- **Owner segment** \u2014 `OwnerSegment`/`Locality.ofMemberId`/`Timezone.ofMemberId` parse the region as the leading letter-run of the memberId.\n- **Fiscal-year value** \u2014 `FiscalYear.labelOfMemberId` reads the `FY` segment back off the memberId, so `fiscalYear` and the id can't disagree.\n- **Audit record** \u2014 `LogOwnerAudit` logs `memberId=` (no more `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`); `OwnerCreatedEvent` renamed its component and JSON key to `memberId` (flowing through `PrimaryIdentifier.of` \u2192 `getMemberId`).\n\nVerified end-to-end: the audit line emitted during the test reads `memberId=NSW2716E6609E1` (region `NSW`, FY `27` for an Aug-2026 registration, hash `16E6609E`, check `1`).",
